# Reason: Ren'Py compiles every python statement and expression when it loads the script (update_bytecode). That was 43 percent of a cold load of a large game, and a Ren'Py 7 game also runs the Python 2 rewrite there. Python statements in label bodies and expressions are now compiled when first used: PyCode.bytecode is a property that compiles a deferred block, and a PyExpr is compiled by py_compile on its first evaluation. Init blocks, python early, define, default, screens and every other holder of a PyCode stay eager, so their syntax errors are still load time errors. A deferred syntax error raises the same ParseError message at the first execution. lint, compile, statements loaded after load_script, and RENPY_LAZY_COMPILE=0 compile everything at once. The blocks compiled after the save at the end of init are written to the bytecode cache when the game exits, and the cache entries of blocks that did not run are carried over, so a warm run stays warm.

